        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "98443b96-7353-574b-8628-139b3276afe4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hovsep Pushman, Armen Chakmakian, John Singer Sargent, George de Forest Brush\n- Organizations: Grand Central Art Galleries, Shadowfax, TruArt Records, GRAMMY Awards\n- Products: Esperanto, Ceremonies, Caravans, Buddha Bar, Buddha Bar IV\n- Places: Glendale, California\n- Topics: Armenian-American artists and musicians\n\nFacts:\n- Hovsep Pushman was born on May 9, 1877, and he was an American artist of Armenian background.\n- Hovsep Pushman was known for contemplative still lifes and sensitive portraits of women, often in exotic dress.\n- In 1928, John Singer Sargent's posthumous show took place at the Grand Central Art Galleries.\n- Hovsep Pushman and George de Forest Brush were closely associated with the Grand Central Art Galleries.\n- Armen John Chakmakian was born on February 11, 1966, in Glendale, California, and he is an Armenian-American musician, composer, recording artist, and producer.\n- Armen Chakmakian was formerly the keyboardist for Shadowfax.\n- Shadowfax's 1992 CD Esperanto was nominated for a Best New Age Album GRAMMY Award.\n- Armen Chakmakian released the solo albums Ceremonies in 1998 and Caravans in 2004 on TruArt Records.\n- Two tracks from Ceremonies, Gypsy Rain and Distant Lands, also appeared on the compilation albums Buddha Bar and Buddha Bar IV, respectively.\n- Hovsep Pushman died on February 13, 1966.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "1b62e653-4404-5daf-8b98-c4ac10d75326",
        "text": "Page: Hovsep Pushman. Sentence: Hovsep Pushman (Armenian: Յովսէփ Փուշման ; May 9, 1877 – February 13, 1966) was an American artist of Armenian background.\nPage: Hovsep Pushman. Sentence: He was known for his contemplative still lifes and sensitive portraits of women, often in exotic dress.\nPage: Armen Chakmakian. Sentence: Armen John Chakmakian (Armenian: Արմեն Չաքմաքյան ; born (February 11, 1966) in Glendale, California) is an Armenian-American musician, composer, recording artist, and producer.\nPage: Armen Chakmakian. Sentence: Formerly the keyboardist for the GRAMMY® award-winning band Shadowfax, their 1992 CD, \"Esperanto\" was nominated for a Best New Age Album GRAMMY® Award.\nPage: Armen Chakmakian. Sentence: He has released two solo albums on his label TruArt Records: \"Ceremonies\" (1998); \"Caravans\" (2004).\nPage: Armen Chakmakian. Sentence: Two tracks from \"Ceremonies\", \"Gypsy Rain\" and \"Distant Lands\", also appear on the famed \"Buddha Bar\" and \"Buddha Bar IV\" compilation albums, respectively.\nPage: Grand Central Art Galleries. Sentence: Artists closely associated with the Grand Central Art Galleries included Hovsep Pushman, George de Forest Brush, and especially Sargent, whose posthumous show took place there in 1928.",
